# Phase 18 client statistics scheduler queue parity

- Recorded: 2026-10-23 20:29:16 UTC
- Workspace: `/Users/bruce.tsai/Projects/trio/rocketmq-classic`
- Starting revision: `ca8aec9f`
- Implemented revision: `644fff21`
- Pinned Java source: RocketMQ 5.5.1, `efa1be59d6fc747ad220f036c86030f05f0419f9`
- Scope: client executor's constructor-time `ConsumerStatsManager` jobs and
  `ScheduledExecutorService.shutdownNow()` returned-list contents

## Finding and change

The pinned `ConsumerStatsManager` constructs five `StatsItemSet`s. Each set
registers six jobs on the shared client executor: fixed-rate samplers at 10
seconds, 10 minutes, and one hour, plus print jobs at the next local minute,
hour, and midnight. The Java pre-start fixture returns 30 such queued entries
along with two submitted delayed futures.

Rust now seeds those 30 real recurring jobs in `OwnedTasks` when the client
control owner is created. Sampling jobs advance metric windows; log jobs retain
their cadence and queue identity, but their callbacks currently emit no stats
log lines. Runtime startup schedules remain separate. A Rust pre-start test
reads `fixtures/runtime/scheduled-executor-shutdown.json`, confirms the same 32
returned handles, and checks the two submitted futures remain pending and
uncancelled after shutdown. The started client scheduler also includes the
stats entries alongside its normal runtime schedules.

